# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "execute {#execute}"
msgstr "execute {#execute}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit.execute` function is not available in Qiskit v1.0. This\n"
"function served as a high-level wrapper around the\n"
"[`transpile`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/compiler#transpile) and\n"
"[`run`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2#run) functions in Qiskit.\n"
"Instead of `qiskit.execute`, use the\n"
"[`transpile`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/compiler#transpile) function followed by\n"
"[`backend.run()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2#run).\n"
msgstr ""
"La fonction `qiskit.execute` n'est pas disponible dans Qiskit 1.0. Cette\n"
"fonction servait de wrapper de haut niveau autour des fonctions\n"
"[`transpile`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/compiler#transpile) et\n"
"[`run`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2#run) de Qiskit.\n"
"À la place de `qiskit.execute`, utilise la fonction\n"
"[`transpile`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/compiler#transpile) suivie de\n"
"[`backend.run()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2#run).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.Sampler)\n"
"primitive is semantically equivalent to the removed `qiskit.execute`\n"
"function. The class\n"
"[`BackendSampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.BackendSampler) is a\n"
"generic wrapper for backends that do not support primitives:\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativement, la primitive [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.Sampler)\n"
"est sémantiquement équivalente à la fonction `qiskit.execute` supprimée.\n"
"La classe\n"
"[`BackendSampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.BackendSampler) est un\n"
"wrapper générique pour les backends qui ne prennent pas en charge les primitives :\n"

